# StencilWrapper

`StencilWrapper` is the positioned box at the root of a stencil. Give it the stencil's position and size in boundary pixels and it places itself there, with `width`, `height` and a `translate3d()` transform. When the cropper runs a transition (after auto-zoom, a rotation or a programmatic change), it animates between the old and the new box frame by frame, in step with the CSS transition of the background image.

```
CropperBackgroundWrapper
├─ CropperBackgroundImage
└─ stencil
   └─ StencilWrapper            (positioned at the crop area)
      └─ BoundingBox …
```

## Usage

Both built-in stencils use it as their root. In a [custom stencil](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil), spread the stencil coordinates into it and pass the cropper's transitions:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { StencilWrapper, getStencilCoordinates, type CropperRef } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	let { cropper }: { cropper: CropperRef } = $props();

	const state = $derived(cropper.getState());
	const box = $derived(getStencilCoordinates(state));
</script>

{#if state}
	<StencilWrapper {...box} transitions={cropper.getTransitions()} class="my-stencil">
		<!-- BoundingBox, DraggableArea, … -->
	</StencilWrapper>
{/if}
```

Without `transitions`, or while they are inactive, the box jumps straight to its new position.

## Props

| Prop          | Type                 | Default | Description                                                                                      |
| ------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `left`        | `number`             | —       | **Required.** The left edge, in pixels from the boundary's left edge.                            |
| `top`         | `number`             | —       | **Required.** The top edge, in pixels from the boundary's top edge.                              |
| `width`       | `number`             | —       | The width in pixels.                                                                             |
| `height`      | `number`             | —       | The height in pixels.                                                                            |
| `transitions` | `CropperTransitions` | —       | The cropper's `getTransitions()`. While `active` is `true`, changes are animated with its `duration` and `timingFunction`. |
| `class`       | `ClassValue`         | —       | Classes for the box. Upstream's `className`.                                                     |
| `children`    | `Snippet`            | —       | The stencil content.                                                                             |

## CSS classes

| Element | Classes                                                                                                     |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Box     | `advanced-cropper-stencil-wrapper`, `advanced-cropper-artificial-transition`, plus your `class`             |

Both base classes only set `will-change: transform`. The animation is done in JavaScript, by the internal `ArtificialTransition` component, rather than with a CSS transition, so the stencil and the image stay in sync even when a new transition starts halfway through the previous one.
